.TH SIG_ACTION 3
.SH NAME
sig_action \- set signal action
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "sig.h"
.PP
.BI "int sig_action(int " sig ", struct sigaction const* " new ", struct sigaction* " old ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sig_action
sets the action for the signal
.I sig
to that specified in
.IR new .
If
.I old
is not NULL, the previous signal action is stored there. This function wraps the system
.BR sigaction (2)
call, applying specific masking and flag policies consistent with the project's signal handling framework.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure.